From de4c9b4d9f22f30e780a5354e15c2ac7ee599a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sam <sam@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:25:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sqlite): node-sqlite3-wasm backend - no native binding,
 no GitHub download

core's SQLite usage (devdata, autocomplete cache, refresh index, docs)
now goes through core/util/sqliteBackend.ts: it prefers the native
sqlite3 driver when its binding is available and transparently falls
back to node-sqlite3-wasm (pure WASM, installed from the npm registry)
when it is not - the last dependency on GitHub-hosted binaries is gone.

- openDatabase() returns a unified promise-based surface (run/get/all/
  exec/prepare/close) normalizing the raw-driver lastID onto run results
- the raw-driver callback/serialize usage (LanceDbIndex, ChunkCodebaseIndex
  transactions) is rewritten on the promise API so both backends work
- sqlite3 + sqlite move to optionalDependencies: their failed install
  scripts no longer abort npm install (the comment-json cascade)
- node-sqlite3-wasm added to core/cli/vscode deps; CLI bundle marks it
  external (its .wasm loads from the real module dir), vscode esbuild
  marks it external + prepackage copies it into out/node_modules
